Prerequisites:

1. Make
2. arm compiler tool chain for v7
3. qemu emulator for emulating the binary
4. linux machine to run all these


Clone the repository:
git clone https://github.com/venu8801/ezRTOS.git

Build instructions:
Run the following commands:

make clean

make all

To run the elf file in qemu use following command:

qemu-system-arm -M stm32vldiscovery -S -gdb tcp::1234 -kernel ezRTOS.elf

✅ using any other terminal connect to multi-arch gdb using the above tcp port ID
add break points and debug the code.

✅ Launch gdb-multiarch
gdb-multiarch ezRTOS.elf
✅ Set architecture (important sometimes)

For Cortex-M3:

set architecture arm

Sometimes GDB auto-detects from ELF correctly, but explicit setting is fine.

✅ Connect to QEMU
target remote :1234

Now you are attached to:

virtual ARM Cortex-M CPU
inside QEMU.
✅ Typical debugging flow
break Reset_Handler
continue

Then:

stepi

or:

info registers




Reach out to me if there are any queries:
email: venu.ark.prasad@gmail.com
